      "created_at": "2014-09-04T04:00:22.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p><a href=\"http://markaaronjames.wix.com/mark-aaron-james-page\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Mark Aaron James</a>, the guy who co-wrote \"Aquaman's Lament\" (the song I used for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wuLLXQizuuY&amp;list=UU4l9kQgaY5wmuW2Lpy-E31Q\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">the last WoW machinima I made back in the day</a>), contacted me recently with a proposal. &nbsp;He wants people to make videos for the songs from his new album and is willing to work with prospective video makers and even share the profits if the videos go viral, for anyone who wants to give it a shot. &nbsp;I told him I'd post a video in my old YouTube channel to get the word out.</p><p>If think you'd like to give video making a try (doesn't have to be machinima like I did, could be live action, stop motion, hand puppets, whatever), <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CeLzBnGhW8U\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">check out Mark's proposal here</a>.</p>",
